                      (    forth6809.asm):09127         ; not restored until this whole test finishes), executes TESTWD
                      (    forth6809.asm):09128         ; (should now behave like DUP), then interprets "ACTION-OF
                      (    forth6809.asm):09129         ; TESTWD" to fetch the current target by name and confirms it
                      (    forth6809.asm):09130         ; matches DUP's own xt. Explicitly forces STATE=0 before both IS
                      (    forth6809.asm):09131         ; and ACTION-OF, since both are documented to behave differently
                      (    forth6809.asm):09132         ; by STATE, same reasoning as TSTVALTO's own TO test.
