                      (    forth6809.asm):15528         ; TSTBACKSLASH - unit test for \. Fake source with SRCLEN=10,
                      (    forth6809.asm):15529         ; TOIN starting partway through at 3 (simulating being midway
                      (    forth6809.asm):15530         ; through a line) - verifies TOIN lands exactly at SRCLEN,
                      (    forth6809.asm):15531         ; consuming the rest of the line. Confirmed via its own code
                      (    forth6809.asm):15532         ; that it reads SRCLEN directly (not a fixed buffer length),
                      (    forth6809.asm):15533         ; matching its own documented "follows SOURCE... operates
                      (    forth6809.asm):15534         ; correctly inside EVALUATE" - this test's own redirect of
                      (    forth6809.asm):15535         ; SRCLEN specifically, rather than relying on the real terminal
                      (    forth6809.asm):15536         ; input buffer's own length, is what actually exercises that.
                      (    forth6809.asm):15537         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
