                      (    forth6809.asm):15911         ; TSTEVALUATE - unit test for EVALUATE. Evaluates the string
                      (    forth6809.asm):15912         ; "1 2 +" (confirmed safe via INTERPRET's own code: it simply
                      (    forth6809.asm):15913         ; stops and returns when input is exhausted, no automatic
                      (    forth6809.asm):15914         ; REFILL, so no blocking risk) - verifies the result (3) lands
                      (    forth6809.asm):15915         ; on the data stack, and that the whole input-source state
                      (    forth6809.asm):15916         ; (SRCADDR/SRCLEN/SRCID/TOIN) is genuinely restored to what it
                      (    forth6809.asm):15917         ; was before the call, not left pointing at the evaluated
                      (    forth6809.asm):15918         ; string. BASE is explicitly saved/set/restored too, per section
                      (    forth6809.asm):15919         ; 3.13's own established lesson, so "1"/"2" parse as decimal
                      (    forth6809.asm):15920         ; regardless of what BASE happened to hold at test time.
                      (    forth6809.asm):15921         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
