C525 DD04             (    forth6809.asm):15940                      STD  LATEST       ; like BASE, is only set by COLD (right
                      (    forth6809.asm):15941                                         ; alongside "BASE=10", in the very same
                      (    forth6809.asm):15942                                         ; init block), which hasn't run yet at
                      (    forth6809.asm):15943                                         ; this whole test framework's own,
                      (    forth6809.asm):15944                                         ; pre-COLD execution point. With
                      (    forth6809.asm):15945                                         ; LATEST=0, FIND reports every word,
                      (    forth6809.asm):15946                                         ; including the real "+" this test
                      (    forth6809.asm):15947                                         ; evaluates, as not found - INTERPRET
                      (    forth6809.asm):15948                                         ; then falls through trying to parse
                      (    forth6809.asm):15949                                         ; "+" as a number, fails that too, and
                      (    forth6809.asm):15950                                         ; throws an error this test never
                      (    forth6809.asm):15951                                         ; catches, landing at THUNCAU's own
                      (    forth6809.asm):15952                                         ; JMP ABORT - which resets the return
                      (    forth6809.asm):15953                                         ; stack, explaining exactly why the
                      (    forth6809.asm):15954                                         ; user's own test run terminated
                      (    forth6809.asm):15955                                         ; without ever reaching TSTENVQUERY1/2/
                      (    forth6809.asm):15956                                         ; 3. The same class of gap as section
                      (    forth6809.asm):15957                                         ; 3.13's own BASE=0 finding, just for a
                      (    forth6809.asm):15958                                         ; different variable this section's
                      (    forth6809.asm):15959                                         ; own EVALUATE test was the first to
                      (    forth6809.asm):15960                                         ; genuinely depend on.
                      (    forth6809.asm):15961         
C527 CC02F7           (    forth6809.asm):15962                      LDD  #TSTCBUF2  ; SECOND BUG FIX: the LATEST fix above
C52A DD08             (    forth6809.asm):15963                      STD  CODEHERE   ; alone didn't resolve this - confirmed
                      (    forth6809.asm):15964                                         ; via a second MAME run (the failure
                      (    forth6809.asm):15965                                         ; persisted, with the terminal output
                      (    forth6809.asm):15966                                         ; varying between runs, a strong sign
                      (    forth6809.asm):15967                                         ; of memory corruption rather than a
                      (    forth6809.asm):15968                                         ; single deterministic missing-value
                      (    forth6809.asm):15969                                         ; problem). Root cause: CODEHERE, like
                      (    forth6809.asm):15970                                         ; BASE and LATEST, is only set by COLD
                      (    forth6809.asm):15971                                         ; and was never redirected by this
                      (    forth6809.asm):15972                                         ; test at all - unlike every other
                      (    forth6809.asm):15973                                         ; test in this whole session involving
                      (    forth6809.asm):15974                                         ; WORD (which EVALUATE's own internal
                      (    forth6809.asm):15975                                         ; JSR INTERPRET calls repeatedly, once
                      (    forth6809.asm):15976                                         ; per token). With CODEHERE=0
                      (    forth6809.asm):15977                                         ; (unredirected), WORD's own write of
                      (    forth6809.asm):15978                                         ; each parsed token's [len][text]
                      (    forth6809.asm):15979                                         ; landed straight at address $0000 -
                      (    forth6809.asm):15980                                         ; which is STATE's own address (offset
                      (    forth6809.asm):15981                                         ; $00, the very first bytes of
                      (    forth6809.asm):15982                                         ; GLOBALS, confirmed by re-reading its
                      (    forth6809.asm):15983                                         ; own RMB declaration directly). Even
                      (    forth6809.asm):15984                                         ; a single-character token like "1"
                      (    forth6809.asm):15985                                         ; overwrites STATE with a nonzero
                      (    forth6809.asm):15986                                         ; value, flipping INTERPRET into
                      (    forth6809.asm):15987                                         ; thinking it's compiling rather than
                      (    forth6809.asm):15988                                         ; interpreting mid-parse - explaining
                      (    forth6809.asm):15989                                         ; both the sequence's own termination
                      (    forth6809.asm):15990                                         ; and why the visible output varied
                      (    forth6809.asm):15991                                         ; between runs (the exact corruption
                      (    forth6809.asm):15992                                         ; pattern depends on residual memory
                      (    forth6809.asm):15993                                         ; state from whatever ran immediately
                      (    forth6809.asm):15994                                         ; before). Redirected to TSTCBUF2, not
                      (    forth6809.asm):15995                                         ; TSTCBUF, specifically because TSTCBUF
                      (    forth6809.asm):15996                                         ; already holds this test's own source
                      (    forth6809.asm):15997                                         ; string ("1 2 +") - redirecting to the
                      (    forth6809.asm):15998                                         ; same buffer would let WORD overwrite
                      (    forth6809.asm):15999                                         ; the very source text still being
                      (    forth6809.asm):16000                                         ; parsed.
                      (    forth6809.asm):16001         
