                      (    forth6809.asm):19454                                   ; (a real discard of the loop-control frame).
                      (    forth6809.asm):19455                                   ; EXIT's own EXITUNLOOP mechanism already
                      (    forth6809.asm):19456                                   ; discards the frame automatically and
                      (    forth6809.asm):19457                                   ; correctly on every path - traced and
                      (    forth6809.asm):19458                                   ; confirmed: with no enclosing DO (compiled
                      (    forth6809.asm):19459                                   ; count 0), with one enclosing DO and no
                      (    forth6809.asm):19460                                   ; prior UNLOOP (discards the full 8-byte
                      (    forth6809.asm):19461                                   ; frame correctly). The one combination that
                      (    forth6809.asm):19462                                   ; broke was UNLOOP immediately before EXIT -
                      (    forth6809.asm):19463                                   ; UNLOOP discarding 6 of the 8 bytes itself,
                      (    forth6809.asm):19464                                   ; then EXITUNLOOP unconditionally discarding
                      (    forth6809.asm):19465                                   ; a full 8 more, overshooting into whatever
                      (    forth6809.asm):19466                                   ; sat below (typically the caller's own
                      (    forth6809.asm):19467                                   ; return address) and branching into random
                      (    forth6809.asm):19468                                   ; memory on return. Since UNLOOP has no
                      (    forth6809.asm):19469                                   ; other legitimate use than immediately
                      (    forth6809.asm):19470                                   ; preceding an exit from the definition, and
                      (    forth6809.asm):19471                                   ; EXIT already handles that correctly on its
                      (    forth6809.asm):19472                                   ; own, UNLOOP is now a true no-op rather than
                      (    forth6809.asm):19473                                   ; a second, conflicting discard mechanism.
