F219 4D               (    forth6809.asm):20615                  TSTA          ; BUG FIX: was a bare "BPL SDPOS" right after
                      (    forth6809.asm):20616                                  ; PULU - PULU doesn't affect condition codes
                      (    forth6809.asm):20617                                  ; on genuine 6809 (same class as TRYNUM's own
                      (    forth6809.asm):20618                                  ; PULU-then-compare fix elsewhere in this
                      (    forth6809.asm):20619                                  ; file), so BPL was testing whatever flags an
                      (    forth6809.asm):20620                                  ; unrelated, earlier instruction happened to
                      (    forth6809.asm):20621                                  ; leave set, not the sign of the value just
                      (    forth6809.asm):20622                                  ; popped. TSTA explicitly tests D's high byte
                      (    forth6809.asm):20623                                  ; (bit 7 of A reflects the full 16-bit value's
                      (    forth6809.asm):20624                                  ; sign) immediately before the branch that
                      (    forth6809.asm):20625                                  ; depends on it. Confirmed via MAME debugger:
                      (    forth6809.asm):20626                                  ; "-123 S>D" returned high cell 0 instead of
                      (    forth6809.asm):20627                                  ; -1 - no sign extension was happening at all.
